From 4d41cbb22260820a0e94abce7757cf17e92c6903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: netplay <netplay@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:32:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Lockstep netplay for SNES: frozen clock, mailbox channel,
 netplay module

clk_emu is clk_sys through cyclonev_clkena; main, the joypad ports, the
block RAMs and the registers between them run on it, so netplay freezes
the whole machine bit-exactly (SPEC.md 10.1). HDMI_FREEZE holds the
picture and keeps sync meanwhile; the SDRAM is refreshed through the
reset path while frozen. rtl/netplay.sv exchanges 12-bit inputs through
a mailbox at 0x3FC00000 (new uncached ddram channel 3) and freezes at
the frame tick when the next input is missing. Cheats, savestates,
turbo, multitap, mouse, Super Scope, piano, SNAC and OSD reset are off
during netplay. OSD option Netplay at status[59:58].

sim: snes_sim --netplay runs two machines with the module, a fake HPS
each and a network with random latency, and compares their CRCs.
